    Found while cross-checking the MCP server's parser against the real captured
    runs. The docs imply a top-level credits field; v0.8.4 nests it at
    run_end.verdict.credits_consumed. Every run was reporting 0 credits.

    Hardened the same code path against a nastier problem in run_end.verdict: on the
    real dark-mode failure Kane classified the bug as 'automation_bug' and suggested
    'Update the test to explicitly turn on dark mode' — i.e. it blamed the test for
    the app's bug. Injecting that would push the agent to weaken ground truth, which
    is the one thing this project forbids. flow_end now carries a headline built
    from the literal failed assertion, and verdict.* is never read.

